        "original_id": "31a78ae9-23ed-5e83-a6cc-4c5196576895",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Manhattan, New York City, Madison Avenue, East 23rd Street, Madison Square Park, Central Park\n- Buildings: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, Met Life Tower, 1 Madison Avenue, 5 Madison Avenue, 432 Park Avenue, Princess Tower\n- Companies: Metropolitan Life Insurance Company, Credit Suisse, Hedden Construction Company\n- Topics: landmark skyscrapers, residential skyscrapers, tallest residential building rankings\n\nFacts:\n- The Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower, also called the Met Life Tower, is a landmark skyscraper on Madison Avenue near East 23rd Street across from Madison Square Park in Manhattan, New York City.\n- Hedden Construction Company is noted for the Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower at One Madison Avenue in New York, New York.\n- Princess Tower was the tallest residential building in the world from 2012 to 2015.\n- In 2015, 432 Park Avenue in New York City overtook Princess Tower as the tallest residential building in the world.\n- 432 Park Avenue is a residential skyscraper in New York City that overlooks Central Park.\n- The hotel in the clock tower portion of the Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower has the address 5 Madison Avenue.\n- The office building covering the rest of the Metropolitan Life Insurance Company Tower block is referred to as 1 Madison Avenue and is occupied primarily by Credit Suisse.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
